# Frontend design schema

Canonical tokens live in `apps/web/src/index.css` under `:root`. Treat that file as the **single source of truth** for surfaces, typography, radius, and default shadows.

Current visual direction: **bright 90s retro** (saturated multi-hue palette, hard offset shadows, display + mono type).

## Tokens (reference)

| Token | Role |
|-------|------|
| `--bg`, `--bg-alt`, `--fg`, `--fg-muted` | Page wash, alt wash, primary text, secondary text |
| `--accent`, `--accent-hover` | Primary actions (hot pink) |
| `--accent-cyan`, `--accent-lime`, `--accent-orange`, `--accent-purple`, `--accent-blue` | Secondary neon accents for chips, horizons, chart fills |
| `--card`, `--card-border`, `--shadow`, `--shadow-sm`, `--shadow-pink`, `--shadow-cyan` | Surfaces, thick borders, hard offset shadows |
| `--radius`, `--radius-sm` | Corner radius (0 for crisp retro squares) |
| `--font`, `--font-display`, `--font-mono` | Space Grotesk / Bungee / IBM Plex Mono |
| `--up`, `--up-bg`, `--down`, `--down-bg` | Market gain/loss meaning colors |
| `--stripe-a` … `--stripe-e` | Brand-bar rainbow stripe colors |

## Rules

1. **Prefer CSS variables** for layout chrome: backgrounds, borders, foreground, accents. Avoid new hard-coded hex/rgb except for **meaning-specific** hues (e.g. market up/down) until those become named tokens in `:root`.
2. **Add new primitives in `:root` first**, then wire components with `var(--…)`—do not scatter one-off palette values across TSX or CSS without a matching token when the color is reused.
3. **Focus**: use `:focus-visible` patterns consistent with globals (cyan outline)—do not remove focus outlines without an accessible replacement.
4. **Consistency**: spacing and component layout follow existing patterns in `app.css`; match established gaps (e.g. `rem`-based grids) unless changing the shell intentionally.
5. **Retro chrome**: prefer thick dark borders + hard offset shadows over soft blur shadows; keep radius at `0` unless intentionally changing the theme.

### Example

```css
/* Good */
.panel {
  background: var(--card);
  border: 3px solid var(--card-border);
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  color: var(--fg);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow);
}

/* Avoid when a semantic token fits */
.panel {
  background: #ffffff;
  color: #2b302b;
}
```

When introducing dark mode later, extend the schema with a class or `prefers-color-scheme` block on the same token names rather than branching colors inside every component.
